Description: EDITION ONLY: take copy-back hardware decoding only by choice
 .
 The edition's automatic default (patch 0054) also took the copying
 methods when the video output could not use the decoder's pictures
 where they are. On an AMD A10-9600P (Carrizo, GFX8), RADV offers no
 VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier, so libplacebo cannot import VA-API
 surfaces, and every film went through vaapi-copy: a GPU blit to a
 staging copy and a read back for each picture, on the GPU that also
 composites the desktop. Frame drops of Life of Pi 3D on its 3D
 television went from 13.7 a minute in software to 427.7.
 .
 The automatic modes now take only methods whose pictures the output
 uses where they are, and decode in software otherwise. A copying method
 is taken when the person chooses it (auto-copy, vaapi-copy and the
 other -copy methods), or where libmedia-gpu-route allows copying back:
 CopyBack=true in group [Decoding] of sparky-stereo-graphicsrc (the
 person's own over the machine's measured record) or
 MEDIA_GPU_ROUTE_COPY_BACK.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
