+                  in Sparky Stereo)
     :auto-unsafe: forcibly enable any hw decoder found (see below)
     :yes:         exactly the same as ``auto``
     :auto-safe:   exactly the same as ``auto``
@@ -1404,6 +1405,16 @@ Video
     combinations of HEVC and Intel chips on Windows tend to cause mpv to crash,
     most likely due to driver bugs.)
 
+    In Sparky Stereo, ``auto``, ``auto-safe``, ``yes`` and ``auto-unsafe``
+    take only methods whose pictures the video output uses where they are, and
+    decode in software otherwise: copying every picture back to system memory
+    costs more than software decoding on some machines. A copying method is
+    taken when you choose it (``auto-copy``, ``vaapi-copy`` and the other
+    ``-copy`` methods), or when ``CopyBack=true`` in group ``[Decoding]`` of
+    ``sparky-stereo-graphicsrc`` (your own in ``~/.config``, over the
+    machine's in ``/etc/xdg``) or the environment variable
+    ``MEDIA_GPU_ROUTE_COPY_BACK`` allows it.
+
     ``auto-unsafe`` is similar to ``auto``, but without the whitelist.
     In general, you should never need to use this beyond debugging or
